course: dictionary
lesson: 10046
title: Words that show strong fear
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Terrified means very, very frightened. You can often work out its meaning from the words around it. «Ruby's friend had been hurting herself on purpose and begged, "Promise me, Rubes." Ruby was terrified.» A friend who hurts herself and begs for a promise would make anyone feel scared and worried, so terrified must mean extremely frightened.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try "Ruby was very, very frightened" and read it again. It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
explain: Terrified can also be the past form of the verb terrify, which means to make someone extremely scared. You can see the verb family: terrify, terrifies, terrified, terrifying. Terrified is the word you use for how someone felt, as in «I'm terrified of spiders».
fact: Terrified means very, very frightened.
fact: Terrified is an adjective, and it is also the past form of the verb terrify.
fact: Terrify means to make someone extremely scared.
fact: People say «terrified of» and «terrified to», as in «terrified of spiders» and «terrified to go in».
fact: «Scared stiff» means about the same as terrified.
exercise: «Ruby's friend had been hurting herself on purpose and begged, "Promise me, Rubes." Ruby was terrified.» What does terrified mean here? | *Very, very frightened | Pleased and proud | Bored and sleepy | Slightly chilly
exercise: «I'm terrified of spiders.» What is the person feeling? | Happy to see spiders | Bored by spiders | *Very scared of spiders | Curious about spider webs
exercise: Terrify means to make someone extremely scared. Which word is the past form of terrify? | terror | terrifying | terrifies | *terrified
test: «The terrified child hid under the bed.» What kind of word is terrified here? | Adverb | *Adjective | Preposition | Noun
test: Which phrase means about the same as terrified? | Very hungry | *Scared stiff | Fast asleep | Calm and cool
exam: Safety lessons teach drills because a terrified person may freeze, so drills help people | *stay calm and act | fall asleep | forget their name | laugh loudly
